Subject: Operator Contract Template V1
Date: 2026-05-26
Operator Template UUID: b8cfbdbf-ce4a-42b1-8f7d-564e03c92b4a

@ [slice_authority] docs/slices/FSC1_Final_Slices.v1.sop
@ [canonical_slice_authority] docs/canonical/LangSOP_FSC1_Final_Slices.canonical.sop
@ [core_schema] docs/schema/Kernel_Record_Core.v1.sop
@ [record_schema_inventory] docs/schema/Authority_Kernel_Record_Schemas.v1.sop
@ [natural_key_matrix] docs/schema/Natural_Key_And_Lifecycle_Matrix.v1.sop

& [OperatorTemplate: OperatorContractTemplateV1] is the common logical contract for compiling stable SOP duties into traceable operators
  + [template_id] is operator-contract-template-v1
  + [template_uuid] is b8cfbdbf-ce4a-42b1-8f7d-564e03c92b4a
  + [slice_id] is FSC1-S03
  + [authority_scope] is operator contract fields, trace shape, preconditions, postconditions, interrupts, faults, blocked output, SOP-first interrupt, and fixture obligations
  + [implementation_scope] is contract template only
  + [input_schema_dependency] is docs/schema/Kernel_Record_Core.v1.sop
  + [input_schema_dependency] is docs/schema/Authority_Kernel_Record_Schemas.v1.sop
  + [input_schema_dependency] is docs/schema/Natural_Key_And_Lifecycle_Matrix.v1.sop

  = must: define operator contracts before any LangGraph node or executable operator implementation
  = must: express success, blocked output, fault output, stale input, ambiguous identity, and authority conflict without hidden writes
  = must: keep operator output as KernelRecord updates, operator_trace records, or SOP-first interrupts
  = must: preserve traceability from source SOP authority to inputs, outputs, and proof fixtures
  - never: implement an operator in this template
  - never: implement LangGraph node behavior in this template
  - never: let an operator mutate source or canonical authority silently

| [OperatorOutcomeKind] is (
  success |
  blocked_output |
  fault_output |
  sop_first_interrupt
)

| [ConditionResult] is (
  passed |
  failed |
  stale |
  ambiguous |
  not_applicable
)

| [InterruptKind] is (
  authority_conflict |
  ambiguous_identity |
  missing_source_lineage |
  missing_proof_route |
  stale_input |
  high_risk_operation |
  unsupported_scope |
  human_override_required
)

| [FaultKind] is (
  invalid_input_shape |
  forbidden_external_dependency |
  hidden_authority_drift |
  false_ready_packet |
  stale_projection |
  unreviewed_completion |
  checkpoint_authority_confusion |
  surface_truth_confusion |
  unsupported_operations_control |
  operator_contract_violation
)

& [OperatorContract] is the required contract shape for one compiled SOP duty
  + [operator_id] is the stable operator identity
  + [operator_version] is the contract version
  + [operator_name] is the human-readable operator name
  + [operator_purpose] is the duty the operator may perform
  + [source_sop_ref] is the SOP authority or canonical artifact that justifies the operator
  + [authority_basis_ref_set] is the signed or proof-backed authority allowing the operator to run
  + [input_record_kind_set] is the allowed KernelRecordKind inputs
  + [output_record_kind_set] is the allowed KernelRecordKind outputs
  + [precondition_set] is the required authority, freshness, identity, lineage, and data-shape conditions before execution
  + [postcondition_set] is the state guaranteed after success
  + [interrupt_condition_set] is the condition set requiring SOP-first or human/deeper-model judgment
  + [fault_condition_set] is the condition set that emits fault_output
  + [blocked_output_contract] is the record shape returned when work cannot safely proceed but no fault is proven
  + [trace_schema] is the OperatorTraceSchema required for every invocation
  + [fixture_set] is the deterministic fixture obligations for the contract
  + [forbidden_scope] is what the operator must not read, write, infer, mutate, or decide

  = must: cite source_sop_ref before operator use
  = must: declare all input and output record kinds before implementation
  = must: declare interrupt_condition_set before implementation
  = must: declare fixture_set before implementation
  = must: reject runtime execution when input records fail common KernelRecord validation
  = must: reject runtime execution when output_record_kind_set includes an undeclared kind

& [OperatorIOBinding] is the relation between operator contracts and kernel records
  + [input_record_kind] is one KernelRecordKind value
  + [input_role] is source, authority, requirement, support, gap, projection, packet, proof, trace, review, coordination, or fault
  + [input_cardinality] is one, zero_or_one, one_or_more, or zero_or_more
  + [output_record_kind] is one KernelRecordKind value
  + [output_role] is create, update_by_supersession, mark_stale, invalidate, contradict, prove, review, or block
  + [write_policy] is create_new_record, supersede_existing_record, append_lineage_edge, or append_review

  = must: prefer create_new_record or supersede_existing_record over silent mutation
  = must: preserve lineage_edge_set for every derived output
  = must: preserve source_ref_set for every claim-bearing output

& [Precondition] is one required condition before an operator may run
  + [precondition_id] is stable within operator_id
  + [precondition_kind] is authority, freshness, identity, lineage, shape, support, proof, ownership, risk, or scope
  + [record_ref] is the input record or set being checked
  + [expected_state] is the required state
  + [failure_result] is blocked_output, fault_output, or sop_first_interrupt
  + [failure_reason] is the reason execution cannot proceed

  = must: classify stale input as stale, blocked, or interrupt before any output is produced
  = must: classify ambiguous identity as sop_first_interrupt unless the operator explicitly handles ambiguity
  = must: classify authority conflict as sop_first_interrupt unless a fault is already proven

& [Postcondition] is one guarantee after successful operator execution
  + [postcondition_id] is stable within operator_id
  + [output_record_ref] is the produced or superseded record
  + [guaranteed_state] is the state after success
  + [lineage_requirement] is the lineage edge that must exist
  + [source_requirement] is the source_ref_set entry that must exist

  = must: be testable by fixture or review
  = must: not promise effects outside output_record_kind_set

& [InterruptCondition] is one condition requiring SOP-first or human/deeper-model judgment
  + [interrupt_id] is stable within operator_id
  + [interrupt_kind] is one InterruptKind value
  + [trigger] is the condition that opens the interrupt
  + [required_context] is the records, sources, and traces needed for judgment
  + [resume_condition] is the accepted decision, source change, proof, or human override that allows continuation

  = must: pause operator flow when triggered
  = must: preserve interrupt context in operator_trace
  = must: return to SOP-first handling for semantic ambiguity, authority mutation, high-risk operation, or missing proof route

& [FaultCondition] is one condition that emits a fault_record
  + [fault_condition_id] is stable within operator_id
  + [fault_kind] is one FaultKind value
  + [trigger] is the evidence proving the fault
  + [fault_output_kind] is fault_record
  + [local_repair] is the bounded repair or blocker route when known
  + [escalation_path] is the SOP-first or manager route for unresolved faults

  = must: emit fault_record rather than hide unsafe unknown states
  = must: block runtime escalation when critical fault conditions are active
  = must: preserve prevention_story when a fault lesson should become reusable

& [BlockedOutputContract] is the non-fault stop result for an operator
  + [outcome_kind] is blocked_output
  + [blocked_reason] is the unresolved condition preventing safe success
  + [blocked_record_kind] is support_gap, work_packet, readiness_projection, completion_review, or fault_record when appropriate
  + [required_resolution] is the support, source, proof, identity, authority, or review needed before retry
  + [retry_rule] is when the operator may be retried

  = must: use blocked_output when the operator lacks required support but no fault is proven
  = must: preserve blocked output as a record or reviewable trace
  - never: treat blocked_output as success

& [SOPFirstInterruptContract] is the semantic escape hatch for compiled operators
  + [outcome_kind] is sop_first_interrupt
  + [interrupt_kind] is one InterruptKind value
  + [source_context_ref_set] is the source and authority material needed for reconsideration
  + [operator_context_ref] is the operator_trace record
  + [decision_needed] is the precise unresolved judgment

  = must: activate when meaning, authority, ambiguity, high risk, or source mutation exceeds the operator contract
  = must: preserve enough context for SJS, human review, or deeper model judgment
  = must: resume only after accepted decision, source reprocessing, proof, or scoped human override

& [OperatorTraceSchema] is the required trace shape for every operator invocation
  + [trace_record_kind] is operator_trace
  + [trace_id] is operator_id plus invocation_id
  + [operator_contract_ref] is the operator_contract version used
  + [input_record_ref_set] is every input record read
  + [output_record_ref_set] is every output record produced or superseded
  + [precondition_result_set] is every precondition and its ConditionResult
  + [postcondition_result_set] is every postcondition and its ConditionResult
  + [interrupt_result_set] is every interrupt condition checked or triggered
  + [fault_result_set] is every fault condition checked or triggered
  + [outcome_kind] is one OperatorOutcomeKind value
  + [started_at] is invocation start timestamp or logical event ref
  + [completed_at] is invocation completion timestamp or logical event ref

  = must: exist for success, blocked_output, fault_output, and sop_first_interrupt
  = must: cite operator_contract and input records in source_ref_set
  = must: preserve trace even when execution blocks or faults

& [FixtureObligation] is the required deterministic evidence for an operator contract
  + [fixture_id] is stable within operator_id
  + [fixture_kind] is valid_success, invalid_input_shape, stale_input, blocked_output, fault_output, ambiguous_identity, authority_conflict, missing_source_lineage, or missing_proof_route
  + [input_record_set] is the fixture input records
  + [expected_outcome] is one OperatorOutcomeKind value
  + [expected_output_record_set] is the expected records or explicit absence
  + [expected_trace_assertion_set] is the trace facts that must hold

  = must: include at least one valid_success fixture before implementation
  = must: include stale_input, blocked_output, fault_output, ambiguous_identity, and authority_conflict fixtures for authority-sensitive operators
  = must: prove hidden writes absent by checking output_record_ref_set and lineage_edge_set

& [OperatorContractAcceptanceChecklist] is the FSC1-S03 verification checklist
  + [required_field_present] is operator_id
  + [required_field_present] is source_sop_ref
  + [required_field_present] is input_record_kind_set
  + [required_field_present] is output_record_kind_set
  + [required_field_present] is precondition_set
  + [required_field_present] is postcondition_set
  + [required_field_present] is interrupt_condition_set
  + [required_field_present] is fault_condition_set
  + [required_field_present] is trace_schema
  + [required_field_present] is fixture_set
  + [required_capability] is success result can be represented
  + [required_capability] is blocked output can be represented
  + [required_capability] is fault output can be represented
  + [required_capability] is stale input can be represented
  + [required_capability] is ambiguous identity can be represented
  + [required_capability] is authority conflict can be represented
  + [required_capability] is SOP-first interrupt can be represented
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is executable operator implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is LangGraph node implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is storage backend choice
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is surface rendering

  = must: accept FSC1-S03 only when all checklist items are satisfied
  = must: open FSC1-S04 after this checklist is reviewed in a completion review
  = may: open FSC1-S05 after this checklist because FSC1-S02 and FSC1-S03 then satisfy the storage decision gate
